<%#
  COMPONENT: Entry page

  Purpose:
  - Composes the reusable page TitleBar with one host-neutral entry-content
    component. The shell owns navigation/breadcrumbs; this component owns the
    actual entry-page presentation.

  Inputs / metadata:
  - entryContentPartial: EJS partial path relative to this component.
  - Standard page title model used by titlebar.ejs.

  CTX contract:
  - Does not create or resolve CTX state. The delegated entry-content component
    owns its entry-level CTX binding.

  Embeds / delegates:
  - Delegates title presentation to titlebar.ejs and entry rendering to the
    supplied entryContentPartial.
  - Entry-page composition contains no engine-selection chrome; the current UI contract is canonical.

  Runtime contract:
  - Used for normal PAGE · ENTRY surfaces.
  - POPUP · ENTRY hosts render the same entry-content component directly because
    popup caption/lifecycle are owned by PopupHost.
%>
<section
  class="entry-page-component"
  data-entry-page-component
>
  <%- include('./titlebar') %>


  <div
    class="workspace-content entry-page-content"
    data-entry-page-content
  >
    <%- include(entryContentPartial) %>
  </div>
</section>
